WEBVTT

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:12.429
There <i>is </i>someone--the genius
who's the pride of the school cafeteria...

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.972
Don't tell me... Is it you, Kana?

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.850
Nope! It's Ureshino.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.854
Ureshino... Is she the small one?

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:24.983
Oh, if you call her small to
her face, she won't get mad,

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.569
but she <i>will </i>kill you, so you should be careful.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:29.196
She sounds dangerous.

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:31.865
So why do you think she'd be
able to tell us about the email?

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.743
She knows a whole lot about computers.

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:38.747
Like one of those people in the news...
A hacker, I think?

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.375
There are really people like that?

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.710
We should probably split up into two groups--

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.629
One to investigate the sender of the emails,

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:46.463
"Senri Misono will teach you something important."
One to investigate the sender of the emails,

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.882
"Senri Misono will teach you something important."
and one to talk to Senri Misono.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.427
Hey, hey, you wanna go
to karaoke on the way home?

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:54.388
Sounds good. Everyone's going, right?

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:55.848
Yeah, I'm in!

00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:59.017
"Shiomi"

00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:21.290
<i>Writing down my aspirations</i>

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.042
<i>For the day when they will come true</i>

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:29.381
<i>The time has come when</i>
<i>I want to turn to the page I marked</i>

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:34.845
<i>Although there are things I lose</i>
<i>sight of with everything that happens</i>

00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:36.221
<i>Hey, it's all right</i>

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:40.142
<i>The start I'm embarking on is unexpected</i>

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:42.978
<i>The memory that you couldn't erase</i>

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:45.647
<i>Even that sad memory</i>

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:49.693
<i>I'll give it a different, happier reading</i>

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:55.324
<i>I feel like just that will change everything</i>

00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:56.450
<i>All Right</i>

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.661
<i>So come now, the way you are!</i>

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.497
<i>Don't hide your weak self</i>

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.498
<i>On my Sheep </i>

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:07.169
<i>Let's meet riding on a dream</i>

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:13.091
<i>Even just calling your name as</i>
<i>I write in this book of adventures</i>

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:15.928
<i>I'm not lost anymore</i>

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:19.640
<i>Let's start our journey together</i>

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:27.397
<i>Yes... more of you and me!</i>

00:02:38.242 --> 00:02:38.867
"Episode 3: Lonely Song Princess"

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:42.955
"Episode 3: Lonely Song Princess"
I'm not sure what kind of club the library club is,

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:46.208
but everyone seems to be having a lot of fun.

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.543
Really?

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:51.505
Yeah, I wonder if it's because of Shirasaki?

00:02:51.505 --> 00:02:55.175
Just by being around her,
I feel my spirits brighten, or something...

00:02:56.802 --> 00:03:03.392
Oh, yeah. Shirasaki is already
like a world heritage site to me.

00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:05.143
World heritage of what?

00:03:05.143 --> 00:03:08.480
I wonder... Of virtue, maybe?

00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:15.070
By the way, you're also secretly
on the Suzuki world heritage list.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.113
Of what?

00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:18.532
That's a secret.

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.409
Probably because you
haven't actually thought about it.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:22.536
You could tell?

00:03:23.245 --> 00:03:25.122
You don't have to try that hard.

00:03:26.582 --> 00:03:27.416
Huh?

00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:33.213
As you can see, I'm a bookworm who doesn't
care about the silences in a conversation.

00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:38.802
You pay a lot of attention, huh?

00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:41.555
I see...

00:03:41.555 --> 00:03:45.893
In other words, you want me to investigate
the sender of the mysterious emails.

00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:48.937
Roughly speaking, yes.

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.981
I see, I see.

00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:58.405
I don't mind taking this on,
but what's in it for me?

00:03:58.405 --> 00:04:00.532
We can't really pay you.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:05.245
I wasn't expecting you to.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:10.000
Then... Why don't I ask you to do a job for me?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.462
Preferably something
both annoying and interesting!

00:04:13.462 --> 00:04:15.839
Your inner thoughts are spilling out.

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:16.465
"Appllio Spring Fair"

00:04:16.465 --> 00:04:21.929
"Appllio Spring Fair"
I know, it's almost time for the Appllio Spring Fair.

00:04:21.929 --> 00:04:25.974
If it's all right with you,
can I ask you to pass out flyers for it?

00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:27.809
Pass out flyers, huh?

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:30.354
Yeah, I don't see why not...

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.148
"Music Department"

00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:38.570
Um, is Senri Misono here?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.405
Was Misono here today?

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:44.451
Who knows? She keeps ditching,
so I hardly notice when she's gone.

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:46.954
Misono.

00:04:48.539 --> 00:04:49.957
You're from the library club...

00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:50.749
"Senri Misono will teach you
something important. From the Shepherd."

00:04:50.749 --> 00:04:54.044
What? An email from the Shepherd?

00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:55.337
Yeah.

00:04:55.337 --> 00:04:56.588
This is what it says...

00:04:56.588 --> 00:04:59.132
Do you have any idea what this is about?

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:00.843
Um...

00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:03.762
Misono! Why are you over there?

00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:07.558
What are you doing?
Your special lesson started a long time ago!

00:05:08.851 --> 00:05:12.354
The lesson was supposed to be optional.

00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:14.648
Stop acting like that.

00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:18.110
Even if you have talent, you must
be diligent in your daily practice--

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.654
I'm sorry. There's something I must do.

00:05:21.947 --> 00:05:25.534
Please contact the email address
on the flyer if anything comes up!

00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:35.586
Yeah, well it sounds
like it's not true, but it is!

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:37.129
No, no way, that's definitely a lie.

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:39.882
--I'm telling you, it's true!
--No, it's not!

00:05:43.886 --> 00:05:44.845
Is that true?

00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:47.639
Suzuki, do you only eat meat?

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:49.308
That's right, I'm a carnivore!

00:05:49.308 --> 00:05:51.977
A lot of things grow when you eat meat!

00:05:53.604 --> 00:05:55.606
Not that!

00:05:55.606 --> 00:05:58.859
Well, that part is unfortunate too,

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:01.486
but I mean I want to
grow like in height and stuff.

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:04.072
But just eating meat is unbalanced.

00:06:04.072 --> 00:06:08.660
Yeah, but I balance things out
by drinking vegetable juice.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.913
Well, I guess that works...

00:06:10.913 --> 00:06:14.833
Were you able to contact Misono?

00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:19.129
--Yeah...
--For the record, I hate people like h--

00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:22.049
Excuse me...

00:06:22.049 --> 00:06:22.883
--like her.

00:06:22.883 --> 00:06:24.718
You don't have to say it again.

00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:30.140
Tamamo, you shouldn't hate her
without hearing her side of the story.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:35.687
But don't you think people with
talent should develop their talents more?

00:06:35.687 --> 00:06:42.194
If not, then it's too sad for the
people working hard in the same world.

00:06:43.529 --> 00:06:46.740
So, what happened with Misono?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.535
I think I'm going to try to go see her again.

00:06:49.535 --> 00:06:51.328
What about on your end, Kakei?

00:06:51.328 --> 00:06:55.332
She said she'd look into the email,
but we have to do something for her in return.

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:56.708
"Appllio Spring Fair" "Special Spring Millefeuille"

00:06:58.544 --> 00:07:01.046
"Special project for the new academic year"...

00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:03.090
"Passing out flyers in costume"...

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.759
"You might even get a glance," it says?

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:08.303
Where are we going to get costumes?

00:07:08.303 --> 00:07:10.931
It looks like Appllio will provide them.

00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:14.309
I've got it!

00:07:14.309 --> 00:07:17.354
All I have to do is choose
something that's not too flashy!

00:07:17.354 --> 00:07:20.190
Tamamo, I know it's embarrassing,

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.443
but if we don't stand out, we won't
be able to pass out as many flyers.

00:07:24.736 --> 00:07:26.780
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:31.034
If the costumes aren't
too extreme, I want to do it.

00:07:31.034 --> 00:07:35.789
Someone actually has a job
for us, so I want to do it well.

00:07:35.789 --> 00:07:37.875
I don't mind either.

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:41.253
I'm pretty okay with stuff like this.

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:44.423
It is my job to support Shirasaki.

00:07:44.423 --> 00:07:47.634
Besides, I definitely want
the information about the email.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:51.054
If the girls are okay with it,
then there's no problem.

00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:56.518
Yeah. Even if guys wear costumes,
it's not like that much is exposed.

00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:59.479
Huh? This doesn't have
anything to do with us, does it?

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.231
In your dreams.

00:08:01.231 --> 00:08:03.192
Of course you'll be wearing
a costume, too, Kakei.

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:06.945
But... I have books to read...

00:08:06.945 --> 00:08:10.782
I'm looking forward to
seeing you in costume, Kakei!

00:08:10.782 --> 00:08:12.326
Was she even listening?

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:15.204
What about the guys' costumes?

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:18.040
Apparently, there's one butler outfit.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.791
So we need one more...

00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:22.252
If it's okay with you guys, I can make one.

00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:24.421
What? You know how?

00:08:24.421 --> 00:08:27.007
Yeah. So...

00:08:27.007 --> 00:08:29.218
Kakei...

00:08:29.218 --> 00:08:31.595
Will you take off your shirt?

00:08:31.595 --> 00:08:35.349
Jeez, how many times do
I have to tell them to be quiet?

00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:44.024
Kakei, don't move...
or I won't be able to do it.

00:08:44.024 --> 00:08:46.109
Uh, right...

00:08:47.236 --> 00:08:50.781
It's my first time doing it for a guy...

00:08:50.781 --> 00:08:52.824
I'm kind of nervous...

00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:58.789
Sorry, did I touch someplace weird?

00:08:58.789 --> 00:09:01.250
No... keep going...

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.961
Wait, wait, wait!

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.049
Kakei...

00:09:09.049 --> 00:09:10.717
Shirasaki...

00:09:15.055 --> 00:09:19.184
It might sound indecent, but it's
cliché to think it's what it sounds like.

00:09:19.184 --> 00:09:21.520
All right, I'm game.

00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:25.482
You guys! What are you do--huh?!

00:09:30.112 --> 00:09:33.407
They really <i>were </i>doing something indecent?!

00:09:33.407 --> 00:09:36.159
Sorry for the interruption!

00:09:37.953 --> 00:09:38.829
Huh?

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:40.205
Hm?

00:09:49.047 --> 00:09:50.299
Thanks a bunch!

00:09:50.299 --> 00:09:52.718
I didn't think it was supposed
to rain until tomorrow.

00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:05.063
Man...

00:10:06.315 --> 00:10:08.317
I'm all wet...

00:10:17.367 --> 00:10:19.578
Why are you here?

00:10:19.578 --> 00:10:22.456
What do you mean why? I live here.

00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:23.332
Huh?

00:10:23.332 --> 00:10:25.125
What, what's wrong?

00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:27.628
This is where <i>I </i>live...

00:10:27.628 --> 00:10:29.004
What?

00:10:30.172 --> 00:10:32.758
Oh, we're neighbors!

00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:37.179
It was so quiet, I thought
no one lived next door.

00:10:37.179 --> 00:10:39.681
Really?

00:10:39.681 --> 00:10:41.016
Nagi...

00:10:41.016 --> 00:10:43.018
Huh?

00:10:43.018 --> 00:10:46.813
I'm Nagi Kodachi. You can just call me Nagi.

00:10:46.813 --> 00:10:47.731
Nice to meet you.

00:10:47.731 --> 00:10:50.984
"Nagi Kodachi"

00:10:51.527 --> 00:10:54.071
Nice to meet you, too.

00:10:56.615 --> 00:10:58.784
You like polka dots?

00:10:58.784 --> 00:10:59.451
Huh?

00:10:59.451 --> 00:11:02.454
Uh, never mind.

00:11:02.454 --> 00:11:04.957
Well, good night, then.

00:11:04.957 --> 00:11:07.251
Yeah, good night.

00:11:11.171 --> 00:11:13.257
What was I expecting?

00:11:13.257 --> 00:11:16.468
There's no way he'd remember my name...

00:11:18.637 --> 00:11:21.390
Woah, it's totally see-through!

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.850
Be quiet!

00:11:37.322 --> 00:11:39.157
This is the arson and theft police!

00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:43.036
Come quietly and no one will get hurt!

00:12:05.601 --> 00:12:07.477
Huh? Whose is this?

00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:11.732
It's yours. Shirasaki made one for all of us.

00:12:11.732 --> 00:12:13.734
Really?

00:12:13.734 --> 00:12:15.986
What is this? An owl?

00:12:15.986 --> 00:12:17.654
It's a hawk. A hawk.

00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:19.656
It's how I imagine you.

00:12:19.656 --> 00:12:22.409
I'm a hawk, huh?

00:12:22.409 --> 00:12:24.369
You don't like it?

00:12:24.369 --> 00:12:27.247
Oh, that's not it. Thanks.

00:12:28.207 --> 00:12:30.834
Shirasaki's an alpaca, huh?

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:33.378
I'm a dog. Woof, woof.

00:12:33.378 --> 00:12:36.173
I'm a raccoon. Yap, yap!

00:12:36.173 --> 00:12:37.841
I'm a fox.

00:12:39.843 --> 00:12:41.553
Wh-What?

00:12:41.553 --> 00:12:44.598
Hey c'mon, c'mere, Sakuraba.

00:12:44.598 --> 00:12:46.767
--C'mon!
--What does the fox say?

00:12:46.767 --> 00:12:47.726
Shut up!

00:12:47.726 --> 00:12:50.270
Anyway, a raccoon doesn't say "yap, yap"--

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.230
Okay, woof, woof!

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:52.564
Yap, yap!

00:12:54.191 --> 00:12:54.983
Woof, woof!

00:12:54.983 --> 00:12:56.276
Yap, yap!

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:57.778
Woof, woof!

00:12:57.778 --> 00:12:58.529
Yap, yap!

00:12:58.529 --> 00:12:59.154
Woof, woof!

00:12:59.154 --> 00:12:59.821
Yap, yap!

00:12:59.821 --> 00:13:02.616
--Woof, woof!
--Oh, what was it again...?

00:13:04.326 --> 00:13:05.953
Yip, yip.

00:13:05.953 --> 00:13:07.704
Oh, she gave in.

00:13:07.704 --> 00:13:10.624
Yes! Thanks.

00:13:10.624 --> 00:13:13.669
A-Are you guys stupid or something?

00:13:13.669 --> 00:13:16.046
Okay, let's commemorate the pillows!

00:13:18.966 --> 00:13:21.218
"Shiomi Happy Project
Won't you make school fun with me?"

00:13:21.218 --> 00:13:23.470
"Please contact me if you would like to help."
"2nd year - Tsugumi Shirasaki"

00:13:34.189 --> 00:13:36.024
The official library club website?

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:36.567
"Shiomi Academy Library Club" "Our Activities"

00:13:36.567 --> 00:13:37.192
"Shiomi Academy Library Club" "Our Activities"
I didn't have much time,

00:13:37.192 --> 00:13:38.735
"Shiomi Academy Library Club" "News Board"
I didn't have much time,

00:13:38.735 --> 00:13:41.780
"Shiomi Academy Library Club" "Contact Form"
so I only put up the bare minimum, though...

00:13:41.822 --> 00:13:43.699
This is amazing!

00:13:43.699 --> 00:13:45.993
Yeah, it's great.

00:13:45.993 --> 00:13:49.788
Well, at least this way the
library club has a public face.

00:13:49.788 --> 00:13:52.499
Yeah! Thanks, Tamamo!

00:13:55.502 --> 00:13:57.421
I don't know this email address...

00:13:58.797 --> 00:13:59.840
"This is Misono.
Do you know how to make porridge?"

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.425
It's from Misono...

00:14:03.844 --> 00:14:07.055
This is it, right? Kannazuki Dorm, Building A.

00:14:07.055 --> 00:14:09.808
Please wait here, you guys.

00:14:09.808 --> 00:14:12.811
"Senri Misono"

00:14:15.814 --> 00:14:17.691
Maybe she's not home.

00:14:17.691 --> 00:14:19.985
You should be worried about something else.

00:14:19.985 --> 00:14:20.819
Huh?

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:23.071
She might not be able to get up.

00:14:24.072 --> 00:14:25.532
It wasn't locked.

00:14:25.532 --> 00:14:28.035
Tamamo...

00:14:28.035 --> 00:14:30.621
It's the arson and theft police! We're going in!

00:14:38.253 --> 00:14:39.880
Misono!

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.135
She's really feverish...

00:14:45.135 --> 00:14:47.971
Tamamo! Kana! Prepare a towel and some water!

00:14:47.971 --> 00:14:49.014
--Got it.
--All right!

00:14:49.014 --> 00:14:51.016
Why...?

00:14:51.016 --> 00:14:52.935
You sent me a message, remember?

00:14:52.935 --> 00:14:54.895
But...

00:14:54.895 --> 00:14:57.397
We have to take care of
each other when we're sick.

00:15:01.276 --> 00:15:02.986
"Kokumi Drugstore"

00:15:02.986 --> 00:15:06.573
I can't believe Misono is down with a cold...

00:15:06.573 --> 00:15:10.077
A lot of the new students
get sick this time of year.

00:15:10.077 --> 00:15:13.997
If you think about it,
we're already second-years, huh?

00:15:13.997 --> 00:15:18.794
I wanted to ask you... Are you done with karate?

00:15:18.794 --> 00:15:20.921
I'm not thinking about a comeback anymore.

00:15:20.921 --> 00:15:23.340
But your injury is completely healed, isn't it?

00:15:26.343 --> 00:15:29.471
There's no such thing as a fully healed injury.

00:15:34.309 --> 00:15:38.605
What about you? What are you
gonna do about the Happy Project?

00:15:40.315 --> 00:15:42.150
Decision still pending, I guess.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:48.156
Oh, I thought for sure you'd be done
with it after the "being nice" period ended.

00:15:50.868 --> 00:15:51.577
"Senri Misono"

00:15:51.577 --> 00:15:56.290
Kakei, Takamine. Thanks for getting everything.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.041
It was no problem at all.

00:15:58.041 --> 00:16:00.460
How is Misono?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.754
It looks like she's a little better now.

00:16:05.841 --> 00:16:09.511
She just looks like a
normal cute girl like this.

00:16:17.561 --> 00:16:21.815
I held her hand thinking
it'd just be until she fell asleep...

00:16:21.815 --> 00:16:24.818
...but she won't let go now.

00:16:24.818 --> 00:16:28.155
Having too strong of a healing
power is a problem sometimes.

00:16:34.453 --> 00:16:36.830
M-Misono?

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.292
Mom... Don't go...

00:16:44.129 --> 00:16:47.216
Oh, I won't go anywhere.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.814
We're going to stay the
night to take care of her.

00:17:02.814 --> 00:17:05.609
You useless boys should go home.

00:17:22.042 --> 00:17:27.756
"We're doing fine. Misono seems
better and is sleeping soundly.

00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:30.425
I hope her fever goes down tomorrow.

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:33.846
Well, see you later. DJ Tsugumi."

00:17:33.846 --> 00:17:35.806
"DJ Tsugumi"?

00:17:36.849 --> 00:17:38.267
Sakuraba?

00:17:38.267 --> 00:17:43.146
"Please play along with
Shirasaki's joke. Good night."

00:17:43.146 --> 00:17:46.108
So that DJ Tsugumi was a joke...?

00:17:46.859 --> 00:17:50.195
I guess things have settled down
enough for her to joke around.

00:18:00.956 --> 00:18:02.916
Don't go...

00:18:10.632 --> 00:18:13.719
So persistent. Who is this solicitor?

00:18:15.554 --> 00:18:18.932
--Hello?
--Hey, hurry up and open the door!

00:18:18.932 --> 00:18:21.393
I don't think I gave you my number.

00:18:21.393 --> 00:18:25.063
It was on the library workers'
blacklist, so I tried calling it.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.736
You're too noisy!

00:18:30.736 --> 00:18:34.031
That's what you get for being a bully.

00:18:36.742 --> 00:18:38.535
Your TV's broken?!

00:18:38.535 --> 00:18:42.789
That's right. And the detective show
I was watching was just about to get good.

00:18:42.789 --> 00:18:43.790
If you don't believe me after I came all this way...

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:44.833
"Natural Spring Water"
If you don't believe me after I came all this way...

00:18:44.833 --> 00:18:49.046
"Natural Spring Water"
You don't cook for yourself at all, do you?

00:18:49.046 --> 00:18:51.089
Oh, I found snacks.

00:18:52.925 --> 00:18:53.800
"Potato Chips"

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.931
Don't make yourself at home!

00:18:59.806 --> 00:19:00.933
Wait, are you--?

00:19:00.933 --> 00:19:02.559
That's right.

00:19:02.559 --> 00:19:06.730
But man, there are books everywhere.

00:19:09.733 --> 00:19:13.946
The library has even more books, doesn't it?

00:19:13.946 --> 00:19:18.742
Speaking of which,
are you and Shirasaki going out?

00:19:18.742 --> 00:19:19.993
Huh?

00:19:19.993 --> 00:19:22.412
I don't care if you guys make out or anything,

00:19:22.412 --> 00:19:24.831
but you should probably choose
where you do it more carefully.

00:19:25.791 --> 00:19:29.127
Are you talking about yesterday...?

00:19:29.127 --> 00:19:33.674
Hey! I was trying not to say it straight out!

00:19:33.674 --> 00:19:35.217
Don't misunderstand!

00:19:35.217 --> 00:19:36.343
That was for my costume--

00:19:36.343 --> 00:19:37.970
What? Costume?

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.430
Just how abnormal <i>are </i>you guys?

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:42.599
You know what... You should let people finish--

00:19:42.599 --> 00:19:44.768
You want me to listen to you? You pervert!

00:19:44.768 --> 00:19:46.812
Get out!

00:19:46.812 --> 00:19:48.772
But this is my room...

00:19:53.402 --> 00:19:57.948
"It looks like the medicine worked,
and Misono's fever is down, too.

00:19:57.948 --> 00:20:01.118
She even ate some food,
so we can stop worrying for now."

00:20:03.579 --> 00:20:05.330
Be quiet! Shut up!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.250
Remember what happened that day!

00:20:11.086 --> 00:20:13.255
Three days ago, right before I met you guys,

00:20:13.255 --> 00:20:15.048
"A new world is waiting for you after school."
Three days ago, right before I met you guys,

00:20:15.591 --> 00:20:17.926
I got this email...

00:20:17.926 --> 00:20:18.802
Misono got an email from the Shepherd, too?

00:20:18.802 --> 00:20:21.346
"Shepherd"
Misono got an email from the Shepherd, too?

00:20:23.765 --> 00:20:26.768
She got it at around the
same time we got ours, huh?

00:20:26.768 --> 00:20:31.231
Doesn't it seem like the
Shepherd is controlling us?

00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:37.738
Sorry I'm late. Ureshino contacted me.

00:20:37.738 --> 00:20:40.574
She figured out information about the sender?

00:20:40.574 --> 00:20:42.868
Yes, here.

00:20:42.868 --> 00:20:47.581
"Here is the information for the person who
owns the phone of the email address in question.

00:20:47.581 --> 00:20:50.876
Normally, you would have to pay first,

00:20:50.876 --> 00:20:53.712
but you can have the info first
since you're first-time customers.

00:20:53.712 --> 00:20:57.257
I'm looking forward to seeing
you pass out flyers in costume."

00:20:59.801 --> 00:21:04.640
So, the owner of the phone
lives in a place like this, huh?

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:09.603
Maybe no one's home...

00:21:09.603 --> 00:21:12.272
What do you want to do? Wait here?

00:21:15.108 --> 00:21:17.152
It opened...

00:21:17.152 --> 00:21:19.488
This situation again?

00:21:19.488 --> 00:21:22.324
No one's lying on the floor this time, right?

00:21:22.324 --> 00:21:24.326
Well...

00:21:28.455 --> 00:21:29.581
What?

00:21:35.254 --> 00:21:39.132
The place was completely deserted...

00:21:50.644 --> 00:21:59.403
<i>The starting bell, the sound of a lock</i>

00:21:59.403 --> 00:22:07.077
<i>While drifting aimlessly, I become an adult</i>

00:22:07.077 --> 00:22:16.920
<i>The time has come when days spent</i>
<i>running and playing seem far away</i>

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:21.175
<i>The answer I gave here</i>

00:22:21.175 --> 00:22:34.104
<i>Oh, if only it had been</i>
<i>passed down somewhere</i>

00:22:34.104 --> 00:22:38.901
<i>For those crowds walking around lost</i>

00:22:38.901 --> 00:22:43.238
<i>It can be a light that shines on them</i>

00:22:43.238 --> 00:22:51.538
<i>On the other side of the</i>
<i>green belt that surrounds us</i>

00:22:51.538 --> 00:22:59.922
<i>You head toward endless tomorrows</i>

00:23:11.975 --> 00:23:16.063
Was I wrong? Was it okay
to go along with her joke?

00:23:16.063 --> 00:23:17.564
You, do it now, yo.

00:23:17.564 --> 00:23:19.274
"Ugh!"
No way! I can't!

00:23:19.274 --> 00:23:22.110
A dog says "woof, woof."
A raccoon says "yap, yap."

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:23.654
Hey, c'mon!

00:23:23.654 --> 00:23:26.573
A dog says "woof, woof."
A raccoon says "yap, yap."

00:23:26.573 --> 00:23:29.326
A fox says "yip, yip," and a cat says "meow."

00:23:29.326 --> 00:23:31.203
Oh, bye Kakei!

00:23:31.203 --> 00:23:33.372
"Next time: A New Library Club"
Hey, stop playing around and go home.

00:23:33.372 --> 00:23:37.088
"Next time: A New Library Club"
No...
